<!--tz-meta {"id":"ruby-changelog","title":"Patchbay — terminal changelog","category":"Ruby","file":"ruby/changelog.html.erb","tags":["ruby","erb","changelog","release-notes"],"description":"Retro-terminal changelog for fictional API gateway Patchbay: every release rendered as a typed terminal session with prompts and a blinking cursor.","dnas":["retro-terminal"]} -->
<% bg = "#0b0f0a" %>
<% ink = "#33ff66" %>
<% accent = "#ffb000" %>
<% muted = "#1f6b3a" %>
<% line = "#33ff6633" %>
<% surface = "#0e140d" %>
<% display = "IBM Plex Mono" %>
<% body = "IBM Plex Mono" %>
<% mono = "IBM Plex Mono" %>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Patchbay — changelog</title>
<meta name="description" content="Patchbay release notes: every version of the API gateway, documented like it happened in your terminal.">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{
  --bg:<%= bg %>; --ink:<%= ink %>; --accent:<%= accent %>;
  --muted:<%= muted %>; --line:<%= line %>; --surface:<%= surface %>;
  --ink-2:color-mix(in srgb, var(--ink) 72%, var(--bg));
  --mono:"<%= mono %>",ui-monospace,monospace;
}
*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}
body{background:var(--bg);color:var(--ink);font-family:var(--mono);
     font-size:15px;line-height:1.75;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
::selection{background:var(--accent);color:var(--bg)}
.wrap{max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 clamp(20px,4vw,44px)}
.term{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:var(--surface);
      margin:clamp(32px,5vw,64px) 0;overflow:hidden}
.term-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:12px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.term-bar i{width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--muted);display:block}
.term-bar i:first-child{background:var(--accent)}
.term-bar span{margin-left:10px;font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-2);letter-spacing:.06em}
.term-body{padding:clamp(24px,4vw,44px)}
.cmd{margin-bottom:6px}
.cmd .prompt{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
.cmd .dir{color:var(--ink-2)}
.out{color:var(--ink-2);margin-bottom:4px}
.out b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500}
.ascii{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;line-height:1.35;margin:18px 0;white-space:pre;font-size:12.5px;overflow-x:auto}
.cursor{display:inline-block;width:10px;height:20px;background:var(--ink);
        vertical-align:-4px;animation:blink 1.1s steps(1) infinite}
@keyframes blink{50%{opacity:0}}
.release{border-top:1px dashed var(--line);padding:30px 0}
.rel-head{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px 22px;align-items:baseline;margin-bottom:14px}
.ver{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;font-size:19px}
.date{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:13px}
.tag{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;border:1px solid var(--line);
     border-radius:3px;padding:3px 10px;color:var(--ink-2)}
.tag.major{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent)}
.changes{list-style:none}
.changes li{padding:7px 0 7px 26px;position:relative;color:var(--ink-2)}
.changes li b{color:var(--ink);font-weight:500}
.changes li::before{content:"+";position:absolute;left:4px;color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
.changes li.fix::before{content:"~";color:var(--accent)}
.changes li.breaking::before{content:"!";color:var(--accent)}
.changes li.breaking{color:var(--ink)}
.dep{margin-top:14px;font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);border:1px solid var(--line);
     border-radius:6px;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--bg)}
.dep b{color:var(--accent);font-weight:700}
.nav{display:flex;gap:26px;flex-wrap:wrap;font-size:13.5px;margin:26px 0 8px}
.nav a{color:var(--ink-2);text-decoration:none}
.nav a:hover{color:var(--accent)}
.nav a::before{content:"~/";color:var(--muted)}
.foot{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:34px;padding:22px 0 8px;
      display:flex;justify-content:space-between;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;
      font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ink-2)}
.foot a{color:var(--ink-2);text-decoration:none}
.foot a:hover{color:var(--accent)}
@media (max-width:640px){.ascii{font-size:10px}.term-body{padding:20px}}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){.cursor{animation:none}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
<div class="term">
  <div class="term-bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>patchbay — changelog — 80x24</span></div>
  <div class="term-body">
    <p class="cmd"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="dir">~/patchbay</span> cat CHANGELOG.md</p>
    <p class="ascii" aria-hidden="true"> ___      _   _      _   _
| _ \__ _| |_| |_ __| |_| |__  __ _ _  _
|  _/ _` |  _|  _/ _|  _| '_ \/ _` | || |
|_| \__,_|\__|\__\__|\__|_.__/\__,_|\_, |
                                    |__/</p>
    <p class="out">Release notes for <b>Patchbay</b>, the API gateway that routes first and asks questions later. Newest first. Breaking changes marked <b>!</b> so you can't miss them.</p>
    <nav class="nav" aria-label="Changelog sections">
      <a href="#v4">v4.x</a><a href="#v3">v3.x</a><a href="#v2">v2.x</a><a href="#rss">rss</a><a href="#api">api</a>
    </nav>
    <div class="release" id="v4">
      <p class="cmd"><span class="prompt">$</span> patchbay releases --since 4.0</p>
      <div class="rel-head"><span class="ver">v4.2.0</span><span class="date">2026-09-28</span><span class="tag major">minor</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li><b>Edge routing GA.</b> Requests now route to the nearest of 34 PoPs by default; median latency down 41% in testing.</li>
        <li><b>Retry budgets.</b> Per-route retry budgets with jitter. Set max 3 retries at a 10% budget and stop retry-storming yourself.</li>
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> WebSocket upgrades dropping headers on the Frankfurt PoP.</li>
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> dashboard showing stale certificate expiry dates after renewal.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="rel-head" style="margin-top:26px"><span class="ver">v4.1.0</span><span class="date">2026-08-17</span><span class="tag">minor</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li><b>Request mirroring.</b> Shadow production traffic to staging with one flag. Finally test against reality.</li>
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> gRPC reflection failing behind mTLS.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="rel-head" style="margin-top:26px"><span class="ver">v4.0.0</span><span class="date">2026-06-30</span><span class="tag major">major</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li class="breaking"><b>Config format v2.</b> YAML configs must declare <b>apiVersion: patchbay/v2</b>. The v1 loader is gone; run <b>patchbay migrate</b> first.</li>
        <li><b>HTTP/3 by default.</b> QUIC listeners on every edge node, fallback to HTTP/2 automatic.</li>
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> 14 memory leaks in the long-poll handler. Yes, fourteen. We counted.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="dep"><b>MIGRATION:</b> v3 -&gt; v4 takes about 20 minutes. Back up your routes, run the migrator, watch the diff, deploy. Guide: patchbay.dev/migrate-v4</p>
    </div>

    <div class="release" id="v3">
      <p class="cmd"><span class="prompt">$</span> patchbay releases --since 3.0 --until 4.0</p>
      <div class="rel-head"><span class="ver">v3.9.2</span><span class="date">2026-05-11</span><span class="tag">patch</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> rate limiter miscounting under clock skew greater than 2s.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="rel-head" style="margin-top:26px"><span class="ver">v3.9.0</span><span class="date">2026-03-22</span><span class="tag">minor</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li><b>OpenTelemetry tracing.</b> Every hop emits spans; plug in Jaeger or Honeycomb and watch your request's whole journey.</li>
        <li><b>Canary deploys.</b> Route 1% of traffic to the new upstream, promote or roll back from the CLI.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="rel-head" style="margin-top:26px"><span class="ver">v3.0.0</span><span class="date">2025-11-04</span><span class="tag major">major</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li class="breaking"><b>Auth plugins renamed.</b> <b>jwt-verify</b> is now <b>auth.jwt</b>. Old names warn for one minor, then break.</li>
        <li><b>Hot reload.</b> Config changes apply without dropping connections. The 3 a.m. deploys just got boring.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="release" id="v2">
      <p class="cmd"><span class="prompt">$</span> patchbay releases --since 2.0 --until 3.0</p>
      <div class="rel-head"><span class="ver">v2.4.1</span><span class="date">2025-06-19</span><span class="tag">patch</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li class="fix"><b>Fixed:</b> dashboard login loop on Safari. We are sorry, Safari users. Genuinely.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="rel-head" style="margin-top:26px"><span class="ver">v2.0.0</span><span class="date">2024-09-02</span><span class="tag major">major</span></div>
      <ul class="changes">
        <li><b>The rewrite.</b> Patchbay 2 moved from a single binary to the edge-agent model. Everything got faster; some configs got louder.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="out" style="margin-top:14px">-- end of history. Patchbay 1.x was a shell script and a dream; we don't talk about it. --</p>
    </div>

    <p class="cmd" style="margin-top:30px"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></p>

    <div class="foot" id="api">
      <span>patchbay changelog · generated from git, not marketing</span>
      <span><a href="#rss" id="rss">rss</a> · <a href="#">github</a> · <a href="#">status: all systems normal</a></span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
